  A connected semisimple Lie group $G$ is called a #idx(
    "Lie group",
    "of adjoint type",
  )_group of adjoint type_ if it satisfies either of the following equivalent
  conditions: $cal(X)(T) = Q$ or $Z(G) = {e}$ or
  $pi_1 (G) tilde.equiv pi(Delta_G)$.

  #exercise[For any semisimple Lie algebra $frak(g)$ there exists a unique up to
    an isomorphism group of adjoint type with the tangent algebra $frak(g)$.
    Such a group is the adjoint group $Ad G$ for any connected Lie group $G$
    with the tangent algebra $frak(g)$.] <exc:adjoint-type-group-unique>

  #exercise[Any self-dual irreducible linear representation of a group of
    adjoint type is orthogonal.] <exc:adjoint-type-self-dual-orthogonal>

  #source(212)Let $G$ be a connected semisimple Lie group, $R_1, ..., R_m$ its
  linear representations, $R = R_1 ... R_m$.

  #exercise[The weights of $R$ are of the form $lambda_1 + dots.c + lambda_m$,
    where $lambda_i in Phi_(R_i)$. Then
    $(V_1)_(lambda_1) times.o dots.c times.o (V_m)_(lambda_m) subset
    (V_1 times.o dots.c times.o V_m)_(lambda_1 + dots.c + lambda_m)$.]
  <exc:tensor-product-weights>

