    $v_Lambda = v_(Lambda_1) times.o dots.c times.o v_(Lambda_m)$ is a highest
    vector of $R$.] <exc:tensor-product-highest-vector>

  Suppose $G = G_1 times dots.c times G_m$, where $G_i$'s are simple groups.

  For any irreducible representation $tilde(R)_i: G_i -> GL(V_i)$ we can define
  an irreducible representation $R_i: G -> GL(V_i)$ setting
  $R_i (g_1, ..., g_m) = tilde(R)_i (g_i)$.

  #exercise[Let $tilde(R)_i: G_i -> GL(V_i)$ be an irreducible representation
    for each $i = 1, ..., m$. Then $R_1 ... R_m$ is an irreducible
    representation of $G$ in the space $V_1 times.o dots.c times.o V_m$. Recover
    its highest weight from the highest weights of
    $tilde(R)_i$'s.] <exc:product-group-tensor-irreducible>

  #exercise[Conversely, any irreducible representation of $G$ factors into the
    product of $R_i$'s obtained by the above method from some irreducible
    representations $tilde(R)_i$ of $G_i$. The representations $tilde(R)_i$ are
    determined uniquely.] <exc:product-group-irreducible-factors>

  Let $T^p V$ be the $p$-th tensor power of a vector space $V$. Let $Lambda^p V$
  and $S^p V$ be its exterior and symmetric powers. Any representation
  $R: G -> GL(V)$ induces the $p$-th tensor power $T^p R = R^p$ in the space
  $T^p V$, the $p$-th exterior power $Lambda^p R$ in $Lambda^p V$ and the $p$-th
  symmetric power $S^p R$ in $S^p V$.

  #exercise[$T^2 R tilde.eq Lambda^2 R plus.o S^2 R$. (For $p > 2$ the similar
    statement is false!)] <exc:tensor-square-decomposition>

  #exercise[Find the representations of the tangent algebra $frak(g)$
    corresponding to $Lambda^p R$ and
    $S^p R$.] <exc:tangent-exterior-symmetric-powers>

  #exercise[$V_(lambda_1) and dots.c and V_(lambda_p) subset
    (Lambda^p V)_(lambda_1 + dots.c + lambda_p)$;
    $V_(lambda_1) ... V_(lambda_p) subset
    (S^p V)_(lambda_1 + dots.c + lambda_p)$.]
  <exc:exterior-symmetric-power-weights>

  #exercise[If $v_Lambda$ is a highest vector of $R$, then $v_Lambda^p$ is a
    highest vector of $S^p R$ and its weight is
    $p Lambda$.] <exc:symmetric-power-highest-vector>

  #exercise[Let $R$ be an irreducible representation with the highest weight
    $Lambda$ and ${v_1, ..., v_p}$, where $v_i in V_(lambda_i)$, a linearly
    independent system of its weight vectors with the minimal possible sum
    $sum_(1 <= i <= p) italic("ht")(Lambda - lambda_i)$, where
    $italic("ht")(gamma)$ (the _height_ of a weight $gamma in P$) is the sum of
    coordinates of $gamma$ in the basis consisting of simple roots. Then
    $v_1 and dots.c and v_p$ is a highest vector of
    $Lambda^p R$.] <exc:exterior-power-highest-vector>

